From 8263bf7d9c81c980b154cc6f8918b6c1cef9306d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rob Woolley <rob.woolley@windriver.com>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 17:47:01 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] setup.py: drop setup_requires=['future']

setuptools' legacy setup_requires mechanism (_install_setup_requires /
fetch_build_eggs) unconditionally tries to `pip wheel` the listed
package from PyPI at build time, regardless of what is already staged
in the (native) sysroot. In an offline/network-isolated bitbake build
this fails outright:

  distutils.errors.DistutilsError: Command [...'pip', ..., 'wheel',
  ..., 'future'] returned non-zero exit status 1.
  ERROR: Could not find a version that satisfies the requirement future

future is still listed in install_requires and is provided at build
time via the recipe's DEPENDS on python3-future-native, so dropping
setup_requires only removes the redundant (and here, broken) fetch
path -- it does not change what mavgen actually has available.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Rob Woolley <rob.woolley@windriver.com>
---
 setup.py | 3 ---
 1 file changed, 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/setup.py b/setup.py
index dbcfb87..8d4a571 100644
--- a/setup.py
+++ b/setup.py
@@ -174,9 +174,6 @@ setup (name = 'pymavlink',
             'future',
             'lxml',
        ],
-       setup_requires=[
-           'future'  # future is required by mavgen, included by this file
-       ],
        cmdclass={'build_py': custom_build_py},
        ext_modules = extensions
        )
-- 
